      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The neighborhood’s name honors Jane Locke Weakley, whose family owned the early Lockeland estate in the early 19th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lockeland_Springs",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1905, Lockeland Springs was annexed into the City of Nashville, linking it to the growing metropolis.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lockeland_Springs",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Electric streetcars first linked Lockeland Springs to downtown in 1890, spurring rapid suburban growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lockeland_Springs",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Lockeland Springs Neighborhood Association, founded in 1978, has led historic preservation and community events for over four decades.",
